BIAS LAYOUT FINDING
-------------------
- Device bytes for block0 attn_bias == file bytes == raw stored order
  (gpu==raw 1.0000, gpu==swz 0.0061), reproducible on the 12:10 exe.
- softmax.comp reads the bias LINEARLY as logical [q,k] (no in-kernel swizzle;
  shaders/softmax.comp:55).
- The committed main.cpp (b4e35f1, tree clean) contains a load-time
  fragment_swizzle for H in {1,16} + an M8_DEBUG_BIAS debug print; NEITHER the
  swizzle nor the print manifests at runtime, across two rebuilds including a
  forced main.obj delete + recompile (12:10:46 build compiled main.cpp; device
  still raw at 12:11). Unresolved exe-vs-source anomaly — flagged.
- nr_model semantics = stored order IS fragment order; recover at load
  (docs/m6b-graph-design.md SS A.6 "Storage trap"). The running GPU consumes
  it raw-as-logical, i.e. deviates from nr_model for H in {1,16} blocks
  (b0-4, 23-30, 40-47, 66-70) UNLESS the golden also uses raw. golden.py
  default = match-the-running-chain (raw); M8_BIAS_MODE=swizzle switches to
  nr_model semantics.

